{"id": "EUVD-2026-98681", "enisaUuid": "7b81eb85-d50a-3b67-9005-a25bab34e28e", "description": "Wazuh from 4.0.0 before 4.14.8 contains a race condition in API login throttling that allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass max_login_attempts by sending concurrent requests. Attackers can fire concurrent login bursts to the authenticate and run_as endpoints, each passing the block check before failures are counted, enabling unlimited password guessing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:54:51", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/security/advisories/GHSA-crrg-5qvw-8wjx", "https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/releases/tag/v4.14.8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wazuh-4.0.0-before-4.14.8-api-brute-force-protection-bypass-via-race-condition"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93346"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "38e0ebbc-a155-32b5-9f25-7828baf8ce9f", "product": {"name": "wazuh-manager", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}, "product_version": "4.0.0 <4.14.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "55a3f211-041d-3baf-b10d-411a263895c0", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}], "isExploited": false}